From aa497fef33c340d97cc22f6bfbc1bd29719ab67a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy Fiddaman <illumos@fiddaman.net>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:31:19 +0000
Subject: libstdc++ testsuite: skip tests that cannot pass on illumos

Skip, on illumos, several tests that expect glibc behaviour or glibc
locale data.

* illumos UTF-8 is RFC 3629-style, 4 bytes at most: MB_CUR_MAX is 4 and
  wcrtomb() fails with EILSEQ for 0x20000000, so codecvt::max_length() is
  4 not 6 and wfilebuf::sputc(0x20000000) throws a conversion error.
* The dragonfly model uses the generic messages facet, which has no
  catalog support, so messages<char>::get() returns the msgid.
* In single-byte locales illumos' wchar_t is the byte value, so the euro
  sign of de_DE.ISO8859-15 is L'\xa4', not L'\x20ac' as on glibc.
* Locale data (CLDR-derived) differs from glibc's: de_DE %a is "So.",
  es_ES %a is "dom.", fr_FR %b is "avr.", pt_PT has a U+00A0 thousands
  separator, is_IS D_FMT is "%e.%m.%Y", zh_TW D_FMT is "%Y/%m/%e", ru_RU
  abbreviated weekdays are lower case, es_ES puts the currency symbol last.
* setlocale(LC_ALL, NULL) reports composite locales as "a/b/c/d/e/f" and
  the dragonfly model has six categories, whereas the tests expect glibc's
  "LC_CTYPE=...;" twelve-category form.
* 22_locale/ctype/is/char/wrapped_env.cc #includes 2.cc, which upstream
  already xfails everywhere but glibc because ctype<char> uses the
  process-wide __ctype_mask table on Solaris; give the wrapper the same
  xfail.
* <iso/stdio_iso.h> declares gets() in namespace std whenever a strict C11
  environment is not requested, so `using std::gets;` is not an error on
  illumos.
* illumos ZFS rejects timestamps outside the 32-bit time_t range with
  EOVERFLOW (tmpfs accepts them), so the far-future utimensat() in the
  last_write_time tests fails on -m64 when the test directory is on ZFS.
  Skip the overflow part in that case instead of asserting; this part is
  not illumos-specific and could go upstream.
